24 Nov 2026 - Cohen's kappa
what is Cohen's Kappa?it is a statistical metric that measures how reliably two raters agree when 
evaluating the same thing,while accounting for the possibility that they might agree purely by chance.
Why is it better than just counting how often the scores match?It is better than simply counting how
often the scores match becuase simple agreement ignores random guessing and can therefore overestimate
the true level of consistency between two raters.
what does weighted add and why does it suit 1 to 6 scores?and what is your target?I am aiming for 
substainal kappa between 0.61 and 0.80,since human graders rarely agree perfectly and my ai grader
just needs to match humans about as closely as they match each other,becuase my essay rubric runs from
1 to 6.I will use weighted kappa whcih treats a close call like a 5 versus 6 as a minor miss while
penallizing a wide gap like a 1 versus a 6 much more heavily.

